^SAMPLE = GSM3764558
!Sample_title = SUM149DMSO
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM3764558
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 30 2020
!Sample_submission_date = May 13 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = Jan 30 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = breast cancer cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SUM149
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: DMSO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = index: SI-GA-D1
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = SUM149, SUM159, SUM149R, SUM159R cells were incubated for 12 hr with JQ1 or DMSO treatment.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SUM149, SUM159, SUM149R, SUM159R cells were grown in SUM Medium
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were collected by trypsinization and processed according to the 10xGenomics sample preparation protocol (Chromium Single Cell 3’ v2 Reagent Kit, 10xGenomics).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were constructed according to the 10xGenomics sample preparation protocol (Chromium Single Cell 3’ v2 Reagent Kit, 10xGenomics).
!Sample_data_processing = Single-cell RNA-seq data generated by 10x genomics are preprocessed using the Cell Ranger (https://www.10xgenomics.com/) to obtain the UMI (unique molecular identifier) counts for each gene in each indexed cell type.
!Sample_data_processing = To get a reliable single cell transcriptome dataset, we exclude the cells with less than 200 genes expressed (UMI > 0) or the cells with more than 80% UMIs from mitochondrial genes. The filtered data is then normalized and scaled by using Seurat to remove unwanted source of variations {Lun, 2016 #8526}.
!Sample_data_processing = Read 1 (R1) has a length of 26 bases corresponding to the 10x cell barcode's 16 bases, followed by the UMI's 10 bases. Read 2 (R2) has a length of 98 bases corresponding to biological RNA. Index 1 (I1) contains the sample index sequence information that is incorporated into the i7 index read (8-bp).
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Rdata contains the raw UMI counts in gene level
!Sample_platform_id = GPL11154
!Sample_contact_name = Kornelia,,Polyak
!Sample_contact_email = Kornelia_Polyak@dfci.harvard.edu
